      "content": "hey i've been doing some weird experiments with my synth setup. i was playing this specific cluster of dissonant frequencies—mostly minor seconds and tritones—and the glassware on my desk actually started vibrating in sync even though the volume was pretty low. it felt like the sound wasn't just moving air, but actually hitting a structural resonance in the room. i'm trying to map out the math behind this. if sound can affect physical objects, there has to be a way to calculate the frequency for more abstract bio-electric states too, right?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
